## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical application of phishing-resistant MFA and device-based access in admin contexts, plus rollout, exceptions, and measurable outcomes.

## Key Concepts

- phishing-resistant MFA (FIDO2/WebAuthn)
- passwordless SSO
- device posture (MDM/EMM)
- conditional access rules
- centralized logging (SIEM) and phishing simulations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example simple authorization gate
function allowAccess(user, device) {
  const okUser = user.isAdmin;
  const okDevice = device.isCompliant;
  const okMFA = user.mfaCompletedWithFido2;
  return okUser && okDevice && okMFA;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle a lost FIDO key or key compromise?
- What metrics would you track to gauge phishing-resistant MFA effectiveness?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical analytics isolation in a multi-tenant fintech environment, focusing on tenant boundaries, masking, catalog governance, and IR collaboration.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant analytics boundaries (schemas or secure views)
- Dynamic data masking for PII in dashboards
- ABAC with tenant context for dataset access
- Immutable audit logs and data catalog tagging
- IR playbooks with defined SLAs and measurable metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
function authorize(userTenant, dataset) {
  if (!dataset.tenants.includes(userTenant)) {
    throw new Error('Access denied');
  }
